# A .semgrepignore REPLACES Semgrep's built-in list rather than adding to it,
# so that list comes first, as documented
# (https://docs.semgrep.dev/ignoring-files-folders-code).
.git
.svn
.hg
_darcs
CVS
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js
.env/
.tox/
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/
test/
tests/
testsuite/
*_test.go

# What git does not track is not ours to scan either.
:include .gitignore

# Prose, not code. The shell in a README is an example to read: a throwaway k3s
# needs `--privileged`, a port-forwarded test LoadBalancer answers plain HTTP.
*.md
